// Failure golden: an `else if` chain annotated on a tail rung and not the head.
//
// Each rung of a chain is its own eliminator with its own slot, and checking
// flows outside-in: the head still needs an expected type of its own. An answer
// type further down the chain never reaches it, so the head is refused as the
// check-only form it is.
if false { ret 0 } else if true -> F Integer { ret 1 } else { ret 2 }

//@ expect-diagnostic: case only checks
